      "task_id": "1035a",
      "exercise_number": 1035,
      "source_part": "а",
      "source_excerpt": "一块长方形地的四周筑有围墙，长 $150\\mathrm{m}$，宽 $110\\mathrm{m}$。在这块地中间要划出一块长方形的草畦，它的四边和围墙的距离相等。假设已知草畦的面积是地面积的 $\\frac{4}{11}$，求草畦的长和宽。",
      "domain": "Let t be the common perpendicular setback in metres. A nonempty interior lawn requires 0 <= t < 55; here its positive smaller area also forces t > 0.",
      "model": "(150-2t)(110-2t) = (4/11)*150*110 = 6000.",
      "derivation": [
        "Expanding gives 4t^2-520t+10500=0, hence t^2-130t+2625=0.",
        "(t-25)(t-105)=0, so the algebraic candidates are 25 and 105.",
        "Only t=25 lies in the physical domain. The lawn sides are 150-50=100 and 110-50=60 metres."
      ],
      "answer": {
        "length_m": 100,
        "width_m": 60,
        "area_m2": 6000,
        "setback_m": 25
      },
      "rejections": ["t=105 gives side expressions -60 and -100 metres; their positive product is not a physical rectangle."],
      "geometric_interpretation": "A uniform inward offset removes twice the setback from each original side. Rotating or reflecting the same lawn introduces no additional dimensions.",
      "check_data": {
        "quadratic": [1, -130, 2625],
        "algebraic_roots": [25, 105],
        "admissible_roots": [25],
        "lawn_sides": [100, 60]
      }
    },
    {
      "task_id": "1035b",
      "exercise_number": 1035,
      "source_part": "б",
      "source_excerpt": "长方形地块的面积是 $1200\\mathrm{m}^2$。在地块的长增加 $4\\mathrm{m}$、宽增加 $6\\mathrm{m}$ 以后，它的面积增加 $35\\%$。求地块原来的长和宽。",
      "domain": "L>0 and W>0, in metres. If 'length' is conventionally the longer side, impose L>=W as an additional naming constraint; do not silently impose it on the algebra.",
      "model": "LW=1200 and (L+4)(W+6)=1.35*1200=1620.",
      "derivation": [
        "Subtract LW: 6L+4W+24=420, hence 3L+2W=198.",
        "Substitute W=1200/L: 3L^2-198L+2400=0, or L^2-66L+800=(L-50)(L-16)=0.",
        "For L=50, W=24. For L=16, W=75. Both positive labelled pairs satisfy the stated area changes."
      ],
      "answer": {
        "conventional_length_width_m": [50, 24],
        "all_positive_labelled_pairs_m": [[50, 24], [16, 75]]
      },
      "interpretations": [
        {
          "condition": "The word length denotes the longer original side.",
          "result": "Only L=50, W=24 metres is admissible."
        },
        {
          "condition": "Length and width are assigned labels without an ordering convention.",
          "result": "Also retain L=16, W=75 metres. Its new labelled sides are 20 and 81 metres."
        }
      ],
      "geometric_caveat": "The increments attach to the labels. Replacing (16,75) by (75,16) while keeping +4 on length and +6 on width is not the same solution and fails the change-of-area condition.",
      "check_data": {
        "quadratic": [1, -66, 800],
        "algebraic_roots": [50, 16],
        "positive_pairs": [[50, 24], [16, 75]],
        "ordered_pairs": [[50, 24]]
      }
    },
    {
